course: dictionary
lesson: 1183
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as numbered senses, and the sentence around the word tells you which one the writer means. Context is your best clue.
explain: «Build a tower out of dry spaghetti and marshmallows with a partner, Grace-from-Brownies.» The words tower, spaghetti and marshmallows show an activity, so Brownies must mean a group that does activities, not a chocolate cake.
explain: A capital letter is another clue. A Brownie with a big B is a member of the Girl Guides or Girl Scouts, while a brownie with a small b is usually a cake or a kind elf in old stories. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: A brownie can mean a small square of rich, soft chocolate cake, often with nuts.
fact: A Brownie, with a capital B, is a younger member of the Girl Guides or Girl Scouts.
fact: In folklore, a brownie is a small, kind elf who secretly helps with housework at night.
fact: Brownie points (informal) are imaginary credit for doing something to please someone.
fact: A capital letter and the sentence around the word help you choose the right meaning.
exercise: «We baked a tray of brownies for the bake sale.» What are brownies here? | *A small square of rich, soft chocolate cake | A type of spaghetti | A kind of marshmallow | A shiny metal tray
exercise: Grace-from-Brownies was Ella's partner in the tower activity. What does Brownies mean here? | *A younger member of the Girl Guides or Girl Scouts | A chocolate cake | A prize for building the tallest tower | A small elf who helps at night
exercise: Nadia says, «Helping with the dishes earned me brownie points.» What does brownie points mean? | Points scored in a game of tag | Real chocolate treats given as a reward | A trophy for baking | *Imaginary credit for doing something to please someone
test: In folklore, what does a brownie do? | Sells cakes at the market | Guards the castle gate | *Secretly helps with housework at night | Sings in a choir
test: «Brownies promise to do their best and help other people.» What do Brownies promise? | To win every game | To stay up late | Never to eat cake | *To do their best and help other people
exam: Read «She joined the Brownies on Monday and ate a brownie at the meeting.» Which two meanings of brownie are used? | Brownie points and a Scout's honour | A brownie elf and brownie points | Two chocolate cakes | *A Brownie: a younger Girl Guide, and a brownie: a square of chocolate cake
